{"title":"2026 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>prime number</i> is a positive integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> whose only positive divisors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and itself. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a prime number since it is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and its only positive divisors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c0977227cfb50870eab2caed47b9c922e3339d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq d \\leq 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53d94bb9e03a00a4f4c87ed2eba48362d947fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21d - 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> is a prime number.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53d94bb9e03a00a4f4c87ed2eba48362d947fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21d - 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> factors as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8ae4ba4584743f34d5074d4b7f61e36263df8465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7(\\frac{21}{7}d - \\frac{77}{7}) = 7(3d - 11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"38\" />. Since this must be prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is already a factor, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/9597210d81a01792b24f558bd39d8acac667c6ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d - 11 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d98588329af0077aacef9411a6750891051cc8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d = 1 + 11 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abc5b8f3e6f7d5b6b87189d154571c000b6291c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{12}{3} = \\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53d94bb9e03a00a4f4c87ed2eba48362d947fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21d - 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, as seen above. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53d94bb9e03a00a4f4c87ed2eba48362d947fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21d - 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> must be prime but also is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dca2f6fd4392e394bc4eb43c72074a2d0477f793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21d - 77 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2ea897e47cd67376eafe5778287b63ae4a571c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21d = 7 + 77 = 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e54cca200c096a06e06a670d0cab18a181de6010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{84}{21} = \\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174827\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 100/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 477/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4135/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   20.966      1 2026_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   20.966      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36906:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174827 and revision id 285673. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}